What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../warmth
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Description:
		(RW) Colour mix of a paired cool and warm RT4539 frontlight,
		from 0 (cool chip only) to max_warmth (warm chip only). The
		backlight class device's brightness remains the total
		luminance; a write here re-mixes the current brightness on
		both chips in one update.

		Up to half of max_warmth the warm chip rises beside an
		undimmed cool chip. Above it the cool chip dims while the warm
		chip keeps rising, until the cool chip is switched off at
		max_warmth. A chip leaving the mix starts its fade at once and
		is powered down after it; the write does not wait for the fade.

		Present only on the cool chip of a pair, which is the parent
		of the backlight class device (reachable as
		/sys/class/backlight/<label>/device/warmth). The value is not
		persistent and starts at 0.

What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../max_warmth
Date:		November 2026
